   Sensor Signal Acquisition},
Booktitle = {2023 38TH CONFERENCE ON DESIGN OF CIRCUITS AND INTEGRATED SYSTEMS, DCIS},
Series = {Conference on Design of Circuits and Integrated Systems DCIS},
Year = {2023},
Note = {38th Conference on Design of Circuits and Integrated Systems (DCIS),
   Malaga, SPAIN, NOV 15-17, 2023},
Abstract = {Climatological conditions study has gained interest nowadays due to
   their effect in human life. Air quality evaluation, both indoors and
   outdoors, is an important concern in cities, industries and workplaces.
   Sensors used for this task deliver small signals that need to be cleaned
   and processed on-the-edge. In this paper, the authors present a
   processing system based on a digital Lock-In amplifier for an NDIR CO2
   sensor as part of a multi-sensor instrument capable of measuring
   different meteorological magnitudes.
   Both in space applications or IoT systems, factors such as maximum area,
   processing time and power consumption must be considered. To this
   purpose, two different implementations for the same processing system
   are presented, a purely hardware architecture and a software
   implementation on a soft-core microprocessor, based on the RISC-V, both
   onto a Microsemi FPGA. Performance, resources usage and processing time
   are compared in both implementations in order to study their scalability
   towards a multi-sensor system.},
