   Antwerp, BELGIUM, APR 17-19, 2023},
Abstract = {Due to technology scaling in modern computing platforms, the safety and
   reliability issues have increased tremendously, which often accelerate
   aging, lead to permanent faults, and cause unreliable execution of
   applications. Failure in some computing systems like avionics may cause
   catastrophic consequences. Therefore, managing reliability under all
   circumstances of stress and environmental changes is crucial in all
   abstraction layers, from application to transistor levels. Machine
   learning techniques are recently being employed for dynamic reliability
   estimation and optimization. They can adapt to varying workloads and
   system conditions. This paper presents reliability improvement
   approaches from multiple perspectives-from transistor-level to
   application-level-and discusses their effectiveness and limitations as
   well as open challenges.},
