   Quito, ECUADOR, FEB 28-MAR 03, 2023},
Abstract = {This paper presents an error resilience evaluation when approximate
   storage is employed on the Memory of Reconstructed Frames in the Motion
   Compensation step of VVC decoders. An error injection framework for
   memory operations is defined to simulate approximate storage using a set
   of typical DRAM and SRAM Bit Error Rates. Moreover, the resilience of
   the Motion Compensation is measured considering the final visual quality
   of the decoded frames. Experimental results demonstrate the resilience
   to approximation in the context of VVC decoders' motion compensation and
   indicate the potential of exploiting approximate storage for the Memory
   of Reconstructed Frames.},
