Abstract = {Optimal deployment of deep neural networks (DNNs) on state-of-the-art
   Systems-on-Chips (SoCs) is crucial for tiny machine learning (TinyML) at
   the edge. The complexity of these SoCs makes deployment non-trivial, as
   they typically contain multiple heterogeneous compute cores with
   limited, programmer-managed memory to optimize latency and energy
   efficiency. We propose HTVM - a compiler that merges TVM with DORY to
   maximize the utilization of heterogeneous accelerators and minimize data
   movements. HTVM allows deploying the MLPerfT Tiny suite on DIANA, an SoC
   with a RISC-V CPU, and digital and analog compute-in-memory AI
   accelerators, at 120x improved performance over plain TVM deployment.},
