Note = {IEEE/IAS Industrial and Commercial Power System Asia (IEEE I and CPS
   Asia), Chongqing, PEOPLES R CHINA, JUL 07-09, 2023},
Abstract = {The diversity of smart city scenarios makes it difficult for Internet of
   Things terminals (IoTT) to accurately match their differential demands
   for computing, storage, and communication resources with general-purpose
   MCU chips, leading to resource redundancy and cost increases. Due to the
   lack of resource demand analysis for IoT application scenarios,
   traditional customized chip design methods cannot be directly used for
   the design of IoTT chips. To address this issue, we propose building a
   decoupled atomic service set to analyze the resource demands of
   practical IoT application scenarios. Specifically, we use timed automata
   to model the atomic services of IoTT, characterize the event attributes
   and time constraints of atomic services, and use UPPAAL to verify the
   reachability of the timed automata model of the proposed atomic
   services. Finally, these atomic services are mapped to the resource call
   situation of RISC-V instructions to guide the architecture design of
   specialized chips for IoTT.},
