Abstract = {AS Dennard's law is coming to an end, on-chip power consumption
   reduction and throughput improvement due to technology scaling pose
   serious challenges; workloads of today's applications (such as AI, big
   data, and the IoT) have also reached extremely high levels of complex
   computation. Power dissipation has become the fundamental barrier to
   scale computing performance across all technology platforms. Computation
   at nanoscales requires innovative approaches.},
